{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772634232,"nonce":"uUa0B0AB8iowH+E8ZgonJuOEKDE=","title":"Per-node direction reversal + triangle port symbols for feedback-loop readability","message":"When nodes form feedback loops (output of A → input of B → output of B → input of A), the canvas\nproduces crossing edges or lines that run straight through other nodes, both hard to parse.\n\n## Solution\nAdd a per-node \"reversed\" flag that swaps input/output sides:\n- Inputs move from Position.Left → Position.Right\n- Outputs move from Position.Right → Position.Left\n- Header layout mirrors (label/chevron on right instead of left)\n- Port symbols change from circles to direction-indicating triangles:\n  - Normal nodes: all triangles point right (→ direction of flow)\n  - Reversed nodes: all triangles point left (← direction of flow)\n\nThis lets the user orient a node so its output points toward the thing it feeds, eliminating\nthe need for long backtracking wires in common feedback configurations.\n\n## Related\n- GitHub #48: \"Add vector-style edge routing tools\" — node reversal is listed in that issue's\n  comments as an interim mitigation. This issue tracks it as a fully-implemented feature.\n- Local issue 7d9dcae: Add vector-style edge routing tools","files":null}]}